# i18n & Translations

ALWAYS render user-facing text through the translation system. Never hardcode English/Vietnamese strings in JSX, toasts, validation messages, alerts, or error helpers.

## Where to call

- **Inside React components / hooks** — `const { t } = useTranslation();` then `t("commons.SIGN_IN")`.
- **Outside components** (axios interceptor, util, store middleware, yup schema at module scope) — `import { translate } from "@src/i18n"` and call `translate("validation.EMAIL_INVALID")`.

## Locale files

- `src/i18n/locales/en.json` — English, primary. Used as fallback (`fallbackLng: "en"`).
- `src/i18n/locales/vi.json` — Vietnamese, optional.
- Default: add new keys to `en.json` only. Skip `vi.json` until the user asks for Vietnamese.

## File structure

The locale JSON always has two kinds of top-level groups:

1. `commons` — shared, reusable text across features (button labels, generic nouns/actions). **Required, always present.**
2. `<feature>` — one group per feature/page (`login`, `employee`, `quote`, ...). Add when the feature is built.

Optional cross-cutting top-level groups (use sparingly): `validation` (yup messages), `errors` (api error map).

```json
{
  "commons": {
    "SIGN_IN": "Sign In",
    "PASSWORD": "Password"
  },
  "login": {
    "STAFF_LOGIN": "Staff Login",
    "FORGOT_PASSWORD": "Forgot Password?"
  },
  "validation": {
    "EMAIL_REQUIRED": "Email is required"
  }
}
```

## Key naming

- Group name (top level) — lowercase: `commons`, `login`, `employee`, `validation`.
- Leaf key — `UPPER_SNAKE_CASE`: `SIGN_IN`, `EMAIL_ADDRESS`, `FORGOT_PASSWORD`.
- Value — human-readable English in sentence case (`"Sign In"`, `"Please enter a valid email"`).
- Reuse `commons.*` before adding a feature-specific duplicate.

## Interpolation

Use `{{var}}` placeholders and pass values as an object:

```json
{
  "login": {
    "WELCOME_BACK": "Welcome back, {{name}}",
    "COPYRIGHT": "© {{year}} SimpliNail. All rights reserved."
  }
}
```

```tsx
t("login.WELCOME_BACK", { name: user.name });
t("login.COPYRIGHT", { year: new Date().getFullYear() });
```

Never concatenate translated fragments — define the full sentence as one key with interpolation.

## Validation (yup at module scope)

Yup schemas run at module load, before i18n is necessarily ready. Store the **i18n key** as the yup message, then translate when rendering:

```ts
const schema = yup.object({
  email: yup
    .string()
    .email("validation.EMAIL_INVALID")
    .required("validation.EMAIL_REQUIRED"),
});
```

```tsx
{fieldState.error?.message && (
  <p className="text-xs text-red-500">{t(fieldState.error.message)}</p>
)}
```

## Don'ts

- Don't hardcode display strings (`<button>Sign In</button>`). Use `t("commons.SIGN_IN")`.
- Don't translate file vi.json
- Don't concatenate translated pieces. Use interpolation.
- Don't call `translate(...)` at module top-level scope. Call it lazily inside a function/component.
- Don't add a feature-specific key when `commons.*` already covers the same text.
- Don't put translated text inside `Enum` values or constants — those should stay as keys / IDs.
